# Radiant Summit: "This land enters tapped unless you control two or more basic lands." Turn 5 Bot1 controls a Plains (one
# basic) and a Plateau (the Mountain and Plains types, but not basic, CR 205.4a): one basic is below the two, so its
# Radiant Summit enters tapped - though Bot2, its opponent, controls two basic lands by then. Bot2 with a Plains and a
# Mountain of its own plays the same land on turn 6 and it enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Plateau
Radiant Summit
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mountain
Radiant Summit
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plateau.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Radiant Summit.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Radiant Summit.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Radiant Summit.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Radiant Summit.Tapped = false
